course: dictionary
lesson: 5262
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Josh can be a boy's name, or it can be an old word, a verb, meaning to tease someone in a friendly way. Look at the clues around it to decide.
explain: A capital letter is a clue. «Josh stares at the clock» is about a person, because a name always starts with a capital J. In maths, Josh is just a character in the story.
explain: When josh is a verb, the sentence shows that someone is joking. «I was only joshing» means I was only joking. Nobody is hurt, so the teasing is friendly, not unkind. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Josh is a boy's name, often short for Joshua.
fact: To josh means to tease someone in a friendly, joking way. It is an old word.
fact: Josh is a common name in the USA, Australia and the UK.
fact: «Just joshing» means only joking.
fact: The verb forms are josh, joshes, joshed and joshing.
exercise: «Josh stares at the clock during maths.» In this sentence, what is Josh? | Something to tease | A friendly joke | A type of clock | *A boy in the story
exercise: «He was only joshing when he said that.» What does joshing mean here? | *Only joking, teasing in a friendly way | Running very fast | Falling asleep in class | Shouting angrily at someone
exercise: Which clue shows that Josh is a name and not a verb? | The word sunny | *The capital J at the start | The word clock | The word tablet
test: «A boy in Ohio called Josh watched his tablet until midnight.» What is Josh in this sentence? | To tease someone | A school subject | *A boy's name | A type of tablet
test: Which meaning fits the verb josh? | Stare at the clock | Be very unkind to someone | *Tease someone in a friendly, joking way | Fall asleep in class
exam: «Josh laughed and said, "You're just joshing!"» What does joshing mean? | *Teasing in a friendly way | Walking away from a friend | Crying loudly | Writing a letter
